=== A2. boundary: trade date vs charge date ===
trade 2025-05-13 (Tue) settles 2025-05-14 -> SEC rate 0.00/M, SEC fee 0.0000 (by trade date it would be 27.80/M = 1.3900)
trade 2026-04-02 (Thu) -> 04-03 Good Friday, no settlement -> settles 2026-04-06 (Mon) -> SEC rate 20.60/M; by trade date it would wrongly be 0.00/M
=== B. the TAF cap binds on large share counts ===
2026-06-15 sell 100,000 sh @ 5.00: raw TAF 19.50 -> capped 9.79; SEC fee 10.30
=== C. size versus this lesson's toy commission ===
SEC fee at $20.60 per million = 0.206 bps of sale proceeds (sells only); toy commission = 2 bps each way
round trip at 2026-06-15 on USD 50,000: buy 0 + sell SEC 1.03 + TAF 0.195 = 1.225 USD
=== D. CAT fee: both sides pay, per executed share (prospective CAT Fees only) ===
2025-03-03 1000 sh: buyer's broker 0.0220 + seller's broker 0.0220 USD (CAT Fee 2025-1)
2026-02-02 1000 sh: buyer's broker 0.0000 + seller's broker 0.0000 USD (none invoiced (surplus reserve))
2026-06-15 1000 sh: buyer's broker 0.0010 + seller's broker 0.0010 USD (CAT Fee 2026-1)
2027-01-04 1000 sh: not in this toy's table: read FINRA Rule 6897 / CAT fee filings
vs the 2026-06-15 sale above: SEC fee 1.03 + TAF 0.195 (sell side only) vs CAT 0.001 per side
rule: store fee schedules with effective dates; never hard-code one rate for the whole backtest.
